<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40892" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπισκοτ-έω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκότος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>throw a shadow
				over</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκίαν ᾠκοδόμησεντος αύτην ὥστε
					πᾶσιν ἐπισκοτεῖν τοῖς ἐν τῷ τόπῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					21.158
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τινὶ τῆς θέας</span>
			<i>to be in the way</i> of his seeing, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Euthd.</u>
				274c
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.538e
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ βωμῷ</span> Judeich
				<i>Alterlümervon Hierapolis</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				339
			</span></i>: abs., <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				24.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Polyaen.
				8.23.2
			</span></i>; <i>form a roof</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
				<u>Aut.</u>
				28.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>. metaph.,
				<i>throw darkness</i> or <i>obscurity over</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ κρίσει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					<u>Vit.Hippocr.</u>
					13
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1354b11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς τῆς ψυχῆς ἐπιμελείαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					1.6
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ πρὸς χάριν ῥηθὲν ἐ</span>. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ καθορᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					8.10
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				2.20
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶνος τῷ φρονεῖν ἐπισκοτεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eub.
					135
				</span></i>
			
			= Ophelio <i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. γὰρ τῷ φρονεῖν τὸ λαμβάνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					250
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δ᾽ ἐρᾶν ἐ</span>. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅπασιν, ὡς ἔοικε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					48
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ὀργὴ ἐ. τοῖς λογισμοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Ir.</u>
					p.78
				</span></i>
			 W.:— 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be in the dark</i> or <i>in uncertainty</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπισκοτεόμενος τῇ ἀπειρίῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Praec.</u>
					8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπισκοτεῖσθαι καὶ κωλύεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					2.39.12
				</span></i>
			; <i>to be obscured</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπό</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινος</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				12.25d
			</span></i>.<i><span class="en">
				7
			</span></i>; <i>to be blinded</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς ὄψεις ὑπὸ θεοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					9.4.3
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.62
			</span></i>.</div>
